<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Haifa</h1><p class="st-meta">1100 CE – 1265 CE (approx.) · capital Haifa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small coastal lordship of the Kingdom of Jerusalem at the foot of Mount Carmel.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haifa">Haifa</a> was taken in August 1100 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tancred-prince-of-galilee">Tancred</a> with the help of a Venetian fleet, after a stubborn defence in which its Jewish and Muslim inhabitants fought together. It was then granted as a fief, its first known lord being <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geldemar-carpenel">Geldemar Carpenel</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haifa">Haifa</a> was a modest lordship with a harbour and the farmland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-carmel">Carmel</a> coast, and was at times attached to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-galilee">Principality of Galilee</a>. It was best known for nearby Mount Carmel, where hermits gathered in the 12th century and the Carmelite order took shape in the early 13th century. Little is recorded about its administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haifa">Haifa</a> in 1187; it was regained after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a> and refortified by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> in 1250-1252. In 1265 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> took and destroyed it.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="crusader state, 1100 CE – 1265 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">crusader state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.59%;width:3.28%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1100 CE – 1265 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Haifa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Geldemar Carpenel</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Caiphas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1182&amp;focus=lordship-of-haifa" aria-label="Lordship of Haifa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5577 985 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Haifa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5897 1241L5908 1277M5897 1241L5815 1335"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5815 1335h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5897 1241h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5897 1241h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Haifa. <a href="/atlas?year=1182&amp;focus=lordship-of-haifa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

